  "behavior": [
    "Organization → Steps retains its loading/empty/read failure/retry/newer-refresh/access-loss states and now creates an organization definition and every-type binding atomically through bindCatalogueStep. Scope identity comes from the owning resource context; no free-form organization ID or role-derived grant is used.",
    "Edits update name/default unit/integer allowance only through patchStepDefinition. Codes remain immutable, package values are not written, and successful mutations reread the authoritative catalogue. Default form values are explicit workdays and zero allowance; both initial positions are explicitly10 with existing stable tie-breaking, not a claimed append/reorder operation.",
    "Retirement requires confirmation, explains retained history and code/name reservations, calls retireStepDefinition and renders late step_bound refusal. Code/name conflict drafts survive. Server forbidden/not-member responses decide access.",
    "One synchronous ref owns pending definition writes. The editor lifetime fences late reply callbacks after refresh replaces it. Decimal validation preserves integer hundredths and refuses empty/whitespace rather than converting to zero. User unit choices are narrowed before submission.",
    "Current WorkPackageApi undo/redo step_nodes_in_use refusals now retain the named affected rows/steps/fact families through the plan writer; history code extraction is exhaustive. No retry, reread, journal mutation or server admission policy is added."
  ],
